From: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 02:40:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: hash SOE output by the outer header

airoha_soe_complete_out() sends an ESP packet that the SOE has encoded
through the outer LOCAL_OUT path, with the header of the original
packet restored, including the skb hash of its inner flow or socket.
The SOE has already numbered the packet, and a flow hashing qdisc puts
the inner flows of one SA into different flows and may send a packet
with a newer sequence number ahead of an older one, which the peer
drops once it falls behind its replay window.

Clear the hash so that it is computed from the outer header, whose
ports word holds the SPI, and the packets of one SA share a qdisc flow.
The outer header of an SOE packet is IPv4.

Signed-off-by: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
@@ -2865,6 +2865,11 @@ static bool airoha_soe_complete_out(stru
 	skb->ignore_df = 1;
 	if (sk)
 		skb_set_owner_w(skb, sk);
+	/* The restored header carries the hash of the inner flow or socket.
+	 * Hash the ESP packet by its outer header, which holds the SPI, so
+	 * that flow hashing qdiscs keep the packets of the SA in order.
+	 */
+	skb_clear_hash(skb);
 	net = dev_net(dst->dev);
 	ctx->tx.dst = NULL;
 	ctx->tx.sk = NULL;
